WEBVTT

00:02:57.131 --> 00:03:00.551
Until they were basically
extinct in the wild,

00:03:00.593 --> 00:03:03.971
with only several horses
left in captivity.

00:03:04.388 --> 00:03:09.060
Conservationists have reintroduced
some of those horses since 1960,

00:03:09.101 --> 00:03:10.603
back into the wild.

00:03:10.645 --> 00:03:14.232
But all 2,000 horses all living today

00:03:14.232 --> 00:03:17.568
are again at risk of inbreeding.

00:03:17.985 --> 00:03:21.656
And many scientists
refer to this challenge

00:03:21.697 --> 00:03:23.658
as the extinction vortex,

00:03:23.699 --> 00:03:28.204
when small, fragmented populations
lose genetic variation

00:03:28.204 --> 00:03:33.459
and become at risk
for the vortex of extinction